            "The model then predicts either \\texttt{true} or \\texttt{false}.\n",
            "\n",
            "\n",
            "\\cref{tab:pretrained-results-table} illustrates the results of our model. \n",
            "We compare EMMA against similar VL models --- i.e., single-stream encoder-decoder models like VL-T5 and VL-BART \\citep{cho2021unifying}, UniTab \\citep{yang2022unitab}, and OFA \\citep{wang2022ofa}. Among these models OFA-base achieves state-of-the-art performance, however, it has $1.37\\times$ more parameters than EMMA and is pretrained with nearly double the amount of data. \n",
            "On RefCOCOg, our model achieves competitive performance with UniTAB, even though it is almost half the size. \n",
            "\\citet{cho2021unifying} hypothesize that the reason for the poor performance of VL-BART on RefCOCOg is that the use of absolute positional embeddings leads to memorization during training. However, EMMA achieves competitive performance despite using absolute positional embeddings. We believe this is due to our sampling procedure that takes into account the dataset imbalance in pretraining (see \\cref{appendix:emma-pretrain} for details).\n",
